# Project Overview
This project is an AI-powered web application built for Assignment 10. The main goal was to integrate a free LLM into a functional user interface to solve a practical problem. 

* Chosen Use Case:[e.g., AI Study Assistant / Document Summarizer]
* AI Platform & Model:[e.g., Google Gemini API - gemini-1.5-flash / Groq API - llama3-8b]
* Tech Stack:*Python, Streamlit (or Flask/Gadio), HTML/CSS

---

# Key Observations & Learnings

* Prompt Behavior: Initially, the model gave very long, generic answers. I had to tweak the system prompt to enforce strict constraints (like word limits and specific formatting) to make the output actually useful.
* Latency: The response time varies depending on the model. [e.g., Groq was incredibly fast with minimal delay, while Gemini took an extra second but gave more detailed formatting.]
* UI/UX: Streamlit made it very easy to build the frontend quickly, allowing me to focus more on handling the API requests and managing the session state.

---

# Challenges Faced 

1. API Key Security: I had to make sure the API keys weren't hardcoded into the script to avoid security flags on GitHub. Resolved this by using the `python-dotenv` library to load keys from a local `.env` file.
2. Handling Empty Inputs: If a user clicked submit without typing anything, the API threw an error. I fixed this by adding basic validation checks on the input fields before triggering the model call.
3. Response Formatting:Sometimes the LLM returned raw markdown code blocks inside the text which looked messy on the UI. I had to adjust the system instructions to control the output layout cleanly.

---

# Future Improvements
* Chat Memory: Currently, the app treats every input as a fresh request. I want to implement session state memory so users can have a continuous conversation.
* File Uploads (RAG): Planning to add a PDF parser so users can upload their own notes or college syllabus for the AI to reference directly.
* Cloud Deployment:I want to deploy the app permanently on Streamlit Community Cloud or Render so anyone can test it via a live link.

